      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Instructor.Assistant - Full-Time (26000339) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Instructor.Assistant - Full-Time (26000339) Job Description Faculty.Instructor.Assistant - Full-Time Johnstown Bus Enterprise Economics and Finance - Pennsylvania-Johnstown - ( 26000339 ) The University of Pittsburgh at Johnstown seeks candidates for a full-time appointment in Finance with the expected start date of August 2026. Rank is dependent upon the credentials of the successful candidate, as is appointment or tenure track status. Applicants must hold a master's degree in a relevant field and have experience teaching on the undergraduate level. Those holding a terminal degree and/or certification in Finance, accounting, or economics will be given priority consideration. ABD with a clear completion timeline will be considered. The successful candidate will have a 4/4 teaching load consisting of introductory- and advanced-level courses in Finance, and possibly a related field. The candidate will maintain an active professional development/research agenda, engage in division/university service, and advise/mentor students. Availability to teach day and evening classes is preferred. Interested applicants should include a cover letter, teaching philosophy, curriculum vitae, teaching evaluations, an example of research/professional development, and names of three recommenders. Review of applications will begin on February 16 and continue until position is filled. examples of research/professional development names of three recommenders university transcripts The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Johnstown Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Teaching Statement, Teaching Evaluations, Other (see posting for additional details) Optional Attachments : Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
