    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006314&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty Instructor Adjunct Clinical",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Instructor Adjunct Clinical (26006314) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Instructor Adjunct Clinical (26006314) Job Description Faculty Instructor Adjunct Clinical Johnstown NUHS Nursing - Pennsylvania-Johnstown - ( 26006314 ) Adjunct Clinical Instructor of Nursing Obstetrics The Division of Nursing and Health Sciences at the University of Pittsburgh at Johnstown is seeking applicants for an adjunct clinical nursing instructor position beginning in Spring 2027 to teach in the BSN program with CCNE accreditation.  The undergraduate curriculum of the Pitt School of Nursing combines the latest in clinical theory with traditional nursing values that emphasize holistic patient care and gives students the opportunity to combine a strong theoretical base of biological and behavioral sciences with a foundation in the liberal arts. Primary responsibilities include teaching obstetric clinicals. Master’s degree in nursing or related discipline preferred; Pennsylvania state RN license and Bachelor’s degree in nursing required with expertise in specialty clinical area. The candidate must possess current clinical knowledge and skills and a passion for participating in the education of the next generation of registered nurses. Must have evidence proficiency with technology and commitment to innovative and evidence-based nursing education.  Preference is given to candidates with previous teaching experience at the baccalaureate level and recognition of expertise in the specialty area. The University is especially interested in qualified candidates who can contribute, through their leadership, research, teaching, and/or service, to the diversity and excellence of the academic community. The review will continue until the position is filled. Apply at https://www.join.pitt.edu/ Please include :       1) vita, 2) evidence of successful teaching and scholarship Dr. Dawn Drahnak N/A The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Johnstown Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006199&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty Instructor Adjunct Clinical",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Instructor Adjunct Clinical (26006199) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Instructor Adjunct Clinical (26006199) Job Description Faculty Instructor Adjunct Clinical Johnstown NUHS Nursing - Pennsylvania-Johnstown - ( 26006199 ) Adjunct Clinical Instructor of Respiratory Care The Division of Nursing and Health Sciences at the University of Pittsburgh at Johnstown is seeking applicants for an adjunct respiratory care clinical instructor position beginning in Spring 2027 to teach in the The University of Pittsburgh at Johnstown’s Respiratory Care Program. The program is accredited through the Commission on Accreditation for Respiratory Care (CoARC). The associate degree program's goal is to prepare graduates with demonstrated competence in the cognitive (knowledge), psychomotor (skills), and affective (behavior) learning domains of respiratory care practice as performed by registered respiratory therapists (RRTs). Primary responsibilities include teaching students in the clinical setting. Requirements: Minimum 4-year degree with an active RRT credential. Must exhibit a commitment to teaching excellence at the undergraduate level, currency of clinical practice, and effective oral and written communication skills. The candidate will teach clinical classes. Other responsibilities include maintaining currency in the field of Respiratory Care, engaging students in undergraduate research, maintaining Respiratory Care laboratory and equipment, assisting in accreditation requirements and service to the department and University. Must have demonstrated teaching experience in neonatal, pediatric, and intensive care. Preference is given to candidates with previous teaching experience. The University is especially interested in qualified candidates who can contribute, through their leadership, research, teaching, and/or service, to the diversity and excellence of the academic community. The review will continue until the position is filled. Apply at https://www.join.pitt.edu/ Please send: 1) vita, 2) evidence of successful teaching and scholarship N/A The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Johnstown Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
